{
  "class": "EntityEquipmentPacket",
  "module": "server/play/entity_equipment_packet",
  "module_docs": [
    "Port of",
    "`net.minestom.server.network.packet.server.play.EntityEquipmentPacket`.",
    "",
    "# Deferrals",
    "",
    "**None.** Each stack goes out with the ported",
    "`crate::item::ItemStack::network_type()` \u2014 `ItemStackImpl.networkType`,",
    "which writes the air stack as a single `0` and otherwise the **amount",
    "first**, then the material id, then the component patch through",
    "`crate::component::codecs::MapNetworkType`. Note that Minestom's *other*",
    "item-stack type, `ItemStackTemplate.NETWORK_TYPE`, writes the material id",
    "first instead; `probes/expected/itemstackwireprobe.json` pins both orders,",
    "and this packet uses the `ItemStack` one, as Java does.",
    "",
    "`components()` and `copyWithOperator` are ported through",
    "`ItemStack::text_components` and `ItemStack::copy_with_components`."
  ],
  "struct": {
    "docs": [
      "Java: `record EntityEquipmentPacket(int entityId, Map<EquipmentSlot,",
      "ItemStack> equipments)`.",
      "",
      "`ItemStack` has no `PartialEq` in the port (Java's is identity-based), so",
      "this record derives only `Clone` and `Debug`."
    ],
    "derives": [
      "Clone",
      "Debug"
    ],
    "form": "braced"
  },
  "fields": [
    {
      "name": "entity_id",
      "type": "i32",
      "docs": [
        "Java: `entityId()`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "equipments",
      "type": "Vec<(EquipmentSlot, ItemStack)>",
      "docs": [
        "Java: `equipments()` \u2014 insertion-ordered, as Java's `EnumMap` is."
      ],
      "wire": "entries",
      "put": "write_equipments(buffer, &$);",
      "take": "read_equipments(buffer)"
    }
  ],
  "new": {
